Privilege Escalation via SeImpersonatePrivilege
cmd
```
whoami /priv
```
The output showed SeImpersonatePrivilege was Enabled. This privilege allows a process to impersonate other users who authenticate to it. On Windows Server 2016, IIS service accounts almost always have this privilege enabled by design.
The attack — called a Potato attack — tricks the system into authenticating as NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM, then steals that token. PrintSpoofer is the tool that automates this on Windows Server 2016/2019.

